            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0318" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1/133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tittmann</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-20T13:00:00-05:00">January 20, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Your No. 6, January 18, 5 p.m. The Department entirely approves your efforts
                    to discourage the League Secretariat with regard to the advisability of your
                    presence at The Hague at the time of the meetings of the Organizing Committee.
                    We do not feel that it is <pb facs="0319" n="310" xml:id="pg310"/> either
                    desirable or necessary that anyone from the Consulate proceed to The Hague for
                    this purpose.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
